  = help: `category(s)` makes it a category, in the formula or with `add`
==== d.reg(y ~ x + day)
error[Z0401]: `day` is a Date variable, and a model needs numbers or a category
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:3
  |
2 | d.reg(y ~ x + day)
  |   ^^^ a date or time in the model
  |
  = help: make a number or a category of it with `add` first: `add(days = time_between(start, day))` gives the time since a date, `add(yr = year(day))` its year, and `add(each = category(to(day, Str)))` each value as a level; as `fe:` or `cluster:` the variable serves as it is
==== d.reg(y ~ x, weights: s)
error[Z0401]: `weights:` needs a numeric variable, but `s` is a Str variable
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:3
  |
2 | d.reg(y ~ x, weights: s)
  |   ^^^ not a weight
